"""codec_test_assets.py — tiny synthetic media for the Layer-B decode proof.

Two one-second 440 Hz mono tones, base64'd, played from `data:` URLs so the MP3 and
AAC decode rows do not depend on a third-party site being reachable or on CORS.
`webkitAudioDecodedByteCount` climbing while these play is a decoder receipt, which
`canPlayType` alone can never be (PLAN_codecs.md §6.3 method note).

Regenerate with ffmpeg (kept verbatim so the bytes are reproducible):

    ffmpeg -y -f lavfi -i "sine=frequency=440:duration=1.0:sample_rate=44100" \
           -ac 1 -c:a libmp3lame -b:a 32k tone.mp3
    ffmpeg -y -f lavfi -i "sine=frequency=440:duration=1.0:sample_rate=44100" \
           -ac 1 -c:a aac -b:a 32k -movflags +faststart tone.m4a
    ffmpeg -y -f lavfi -i "testsrc=size=64x64:rate=15:duration=1.0"            -c:v libx264 -profile:v baseline -level 3.0 -pix_fmt yuv420p            -movflags +faststart tone_h264.mp4
    python -c "import base64,sys;print(base64.b64encode(open(sys.argv[1],'rb').read()).decode())" tone.mp3

`tone_h264.mp4` is Constrained Baseline, 64x64, 1 s -- the H.264 half of the decode
receipt, kept local because the public sample MP4 this row used first started answering
403 mid-sprint. A remote asset in a release gate is a row that rots.
"""

MP3_B64 = ""

AAC_M4A_B64 = ""

H264_MP4_B64 = ""

# NEGATIVE CONTROL asset: AC-3 in MP4. ENABLE_PLATFORM_AC3_EAC3_AUDIO is 0 in this
# build, so this MUST fail to decode. It is the row that proves Layer B can go red.
AC3_MP4_B64 = ""
